A||||9||Steven||3.2 rebuild update.||||1||
Z||000000||Steven||06-26-2001||01:26 PM||||Will 500 miles had been logged on the new motor. It was time to open her up, and see what she will do. A friend of mine loaned be his G-Tech Pro. Plugged it in, and set it for the 1/4 mile time. Best run? 14.97 sec. Now I know some people will tell me I should be faster, but I still need to clean the K&N filter, new plug wires, and a better ign. coil. I was also thinking of a new chip, t-stat, and fan switch. Also was thinking of adding a "holly" type scoop on the side, and maybe an underdrive pulley. Will just have to wait and see how the money thing goes. Well tonight I go home and change the oil, wash and wax the car. Maybe I will even put the stickers that came with most of my parts on the under side of the deck lid. Some here said that stickers are good for 1-2 tenths. But that might only be if you show them off.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT<BR>3.2 liter w/4sp manual trans<BR>Silver.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||06-26-2001||05:27 PM||||She hasn’t broken in yet Steve. The more miles you drive the faster it is going to get. <P>If you give me the specifications for your engine I can give you some shift points to try.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||06-26-2001||08:12 PM||||Yes, give it 3,000 miles and then see what happens. <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steven||06-27-2001||04:41 PM||||2.8 liter block, bored .75 mm over, with 3.1 liter crank. Heads are ported and polished (sorry, I did not bench flow them, so I have no numbers there). Stock throttle body, Injector rebuilt by Morran Motor Sports ( <A HREF="http://www.injectors.com" TARGET=_blank>www.injectors.com</A>  ). Cam is a Crane Compucam 2030. To see spec card <A HREF="http://dab7.cranecams.com/SpecCard/DisplayCatalogCard.asp?PN=254122" TARGET=_blank>http://dab7.cranecams.com/SpecCard/DisplayCatalogCard.asp?PN=254122</A>  . If it did not come up go to <A HREF="http://www.cranecams.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cranecams.com</A>  , and choose spec card for the 254122 cam. Ported exhaust manifold, and currently a Walker brand muffler (Walker is the GM replacement muffler) Coil is still stock, and so is the ECM. Anything I missed? Let me know. By the way 88, your parts should be in the mail today, assuming the wife remember that they are in her back seat, she "forgot" yesterday. Of course, that excuse never works for me. Let me know, when you get them. <P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT<BR>3.2 liter w/4sp manual trans<BR>Silver.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||06-27-2001||05:42 PM||||OK here's what I need to know.<BR>Engine, <BR>1. Type of pistons you have<BR>2. Are the exhaust manifolds ported?<BR>3. The Walker muffler is a stock replacement muffler right?<BR>4. Are the intake and exhaust runners larger?<BR>5. What has been polished in the runners?<P>Drag,<BR>1. Vehicle weight including you in it<BR>2. Tire size and type<BR>3. Is the final drive a 3.65 in your four speed?<BR>4. Equivalent elevation in feet within 50 feet<BR>5. Temperature during test runs<BR>6. Approximate humidity during test run<BR>7. Most important I need to know what is the highest launch speed you use without tire spin, if they do spin how much?   <BR> <P>I didn't get your mailing address for the check!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Steven||06-27-2001||06:37 PM||||First thing first. I did not want any money for the parts. Get your Fiero on the road, and take the couple of extra dollars to your favorite gas pump.<P>Now the answers to your questions:<BR>Engine<BR>1.Seal power pistons for a 3.1 Firebird .75 oversized (H562CP)<BR>2.Yes the exhaust manifold is ported.<BR>3.Yes walker is the direct replacement for the stock muffler. (No performance gain.)<BR>4.The runners were gasket matched.<BR>5.The bowls, and runners.<P>Drag<BR>1. 3275 lbs.<BR>2. 15x7 Goodyear Eagle GT II 205-60-15. I think they are H rated if it matters.<BR>3. Trans is still the 3.65.<BR>4. This was hard to find. I went to <A HREF="http://www.askjeeves.com" TARGET=_blank>www.askjeeves.com</A>  and asked what was the elevation was for Grand Blanc, Mi is 839 ft above sea level.<BR>5. Temp was around 85* yesterday<BR>6. Humidity 40-45%<BR>7. Not sure really, I thought I lauched at around 2000 rpm, with mild wheel spin. When I rev higher, the wheels spin like mad. Looks and sounds cool. Does nothing, but hurt the e.t.'s.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT<BR>3.2 liter w/4sp manual trans<BR>Silver.<p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||06-27-2001||07:57 PM||||I ran the numbers and here is what I got. <P>With Dyno2000 I got 168 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 203-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm. With Drapstrip2000 and that engine I got a best 0-60 mph time in 7.167 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.271 seconds @ 91.7 mph. I used a shift time of .150 seconds.<P>If I use a quicker shift time of .125 seconds I get a 0-60 mph in 7 seconds and the quarter mile comes in at 15.1 seconds @ 91.8 mph. <P>I think you have more than 168 horsepower, your cylinder heads must flow real well. The 3275 lb. vehicle weight though is on the heavy side. Are you sure that is right?<P>If I use a 3000 lb. weight I get 0-60 mph in 6.65 seconds and the quarter mile in 14.84 seconds @ 93.9 mph. <P>The shift/launch rpm I used was,<BR>Launch 2200<BR>1-2 6000<BR>2-3 6100<BR>3-4 you’re through the quarter mile <P>Using that same car (3275 lbs.) with the stock 2.8-liter engine I got a best time of 0-60 mph in 8.5 seconds and the quarter mile in 16.1 seconds @ 85.6 mph.<P>What did you get for a horsepower rating on the G-tech?   <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eric||06-27-2001||08:11 PM||||Wow, I just hate this.  I pretty much have the same engine, except for the cam, in my car.  Even with a lighter weight, I'm only pulling high 7 seconds 0-60 and around 16 flat 1/4 mile.  We thought the pistons may be the problem, but now I'm thinking it's the cam.  The car really isn't any better than a stock 2.8.  I didn't build the shortblock myself, so I really don't know if the cam is degreed in right.  I gotta figure this freakin' thing out.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||06-27-2001||08:22 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierodrag4.jpg"> <P><BR>this is a bone stock 86 GT 4spd.<P>How do those times compute into hp with your program?? this car has run a best of 15.2<P>Have I mentioned it totally stock??? <P>George Balzers car. 86 GT 4spd<P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||06-27-2001||08:34 PM||||Slam, for me to give you HP I need some information. I need to know the vehicle weight including you, your launch rpm, 1-2 shift, 2-3, shift and so on. I need the elevation of the track and the approximate temperature that day. Which transmission do you have, 5-speed or 4-speed? I have all of the rest of the information already.   <P>I think you already know what your HP is using the G-tech and your just testing me. That’s OK I'm up to the challenge if you are.<BR>||||reg||1
